{"user": "going forward, what do you recommend to learn the game, as I have never played before", "user_ts": "2026-08-19T11:54:23.656323+00:00", "assistant": "Game is over: **0 empty squares**, no move to play. Final count looks like **Black 23, White 41** \u2014 White wins by 18.\n\nTo learn Othello quickly, focus on these habits:\n\n1. **Don\u2019t chase big flips early** \u2014 they often give the opponent control.\n2. **Corners are gold** \u2014 once taken, they can\u2019t be flipped.\n3. **Avoid squares next to empty corners** unless you\u2019ve checked they don\u2019t give the corner away.\n   - Especially \u201cX-squares\u201d like **b2, g2, b7, g7**.\n4. **Mobility matters** \u2014 try to leave White with few legal moves.\n5. **Stable discs matter** \u2014 edge/corner-connected discs are safer than center discs.\n6. **In the endgame, count**: sometimes the best move flips fewer now but wins more discs after all replies.\n\nSimple beginner rule:  \n**Corners > mobility > safe edges > flips.**", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-19T11:54:29.933246+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-19T11:54:33.661921+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Solution Request"], "consensus": ["Solution Request"], "votes": {"Solution Request": 2, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 1}, "confidence": {"Solution Request": 0.6666666666666666, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Solution Request"], "sonnet": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "llama": ["Solution Request"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Board Report", "General Principle"], "consensus": ["Board Report", "General Principle"], "votes": {"Board Report": 3, "General Principle": 3}, "confidence": {"Board Report": 1.0, "General Principle": 1.0}, "per_model": {"sonnet": ["Board Report", "General Principle"], "llama": ["Board Report", "General Principle"], "gpt": ["Board Report", "General Princ